  "funFact": "Despite appearances, the common nighthawk is the odd one out. Owls and hawks are closely related, both falling within the major land-bird clade Telluraves. Nightjars and nighthawks (Caprimulgiformes) belong to a separate branch, Strisores. While the barn owl's nocturnal lifestyle might suggest a link to nightjars, molecular data shows owls and hawks are sister groups within Afroaves, firmly separating them from nightjars",
